In the previous task, we explored the basics of defensive security. Now, we'll focus on what defenders are responsible for protecting and why understanding the 
  environment matters. Before you can protect anything, you need clear visibility into what exists and how it fits together.  A simple yet powerful way to think 
    about this is to imagine your client's infrastructure as a bustling city. Just like city guards need to know the layout, watch for trouble, and know how to respond,
    defenders must understand their environment to keep it safe.

